{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"morose-selfaware-unicorn","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nProduction rich-text convergence mutates a binding entry reached through shallow `all_bindings()`, bypassing lifecycle policy. The public shallow query must remain compatible, but production needs a named mutation seam.\n\n## Outcome\nAdd `BindingStore.note_rich_emit(local_id, wire)` or an equivalently narrow operation that owns hash/counter/save behavior and returns the current nonfatal missing-binding result. Do not cut over `apply_handlers.py` yet.\n\n## Plan\n1. Capture the current production sequence in a failing comparison test, including changed/unchanged wire hashes, counters, dirty/save gating, and missing binding.\n2. Implement the operation through facade -> lifecycle -> repository while retaining the original dictionaries.\n3. Keep `all_bindings()` copy depth and public signatures unchanged, but document the new method as the supported mutation seam.\n4. Add a boundary test proving adapters and reconciler callers cannot obtain direct writable repository/lifecycle objects.\n\n## Testing\nCompare new-operation results and persisted bytes with the legacy mutation sequence for changed, unchanged, and missing cases.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Changed rich-emission wire data produces the same hash, counter, dirty state, and saved bytes as the legacy sequence.\n- [ ] Unchanged data performs no save.\n- [ ] Missing bindings remain nonfatal with the current result.\n- [ ] `all_bindings()` remains shallow and every existing facade signature remains unchanged.\n- [ ] No production adapter receives direct repository or lifecycle mutation access.\n\n## Out of scope\n`apply_handlers.py` cutover belongs to RP-02 S3 after its RP-04 coordination condition.","id":"2419-2804-c181-4bc0","parent_id":"fc1c-1b08-70c2-4afb","priority":1,"tags":["rp02","binding-lifecycle","tdd"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-02 S2 T3 — Add the narrow rich-emission facade operation"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787027604828265001,"uuid":"3fcc54e0-e6d5-4fed-a3f2-b4cbf0856cc9"}